mfmediaengine: render video into MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_PLAYBACK_HWND (rendering mode)

His words: "tip videos don't play on 2027 as you can see generate image's has a grey box where there should be
content playing" (Photoshop 2027 28.0.0.20, runtime 11.10-203, fresh prefix Adobe2027). On Windows the tip's video plays.

Mechanism (SOLID, lab trace +mfplat on 203):
  Photoshop's feature cards / coach marks are the UXP plugin Required/UXP/com.adobe.photoshop.inAppMessaging; the
  Generate Image card plays assets/gen_image.mp4 (H.264 High 512x288) through a UXP <video>. UXP's runtime
  (dynamic-torqnative.dll, same in PS 2026/2027, InDesign, Animate, AE, Premiere) plays <video> with IMFMediaEngine in
  RENDERING MODE: MFCreateAttributes; SetUINT64(MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_PLAYBACK_HWND, <its child OS_ViewContainer window>);
  SetUnknown(MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_CALLBACK); CreateInstance(MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_WAITFORSTABLE_STATE) -- no
  MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_FORMAT, no DXGI manager; then SetSource(<mp4>), UpdateVideoStream(NULL, dst, border).
  Wine recorded MEDIA_ENGINE_RENDERING_MODE but nothing used it: media_engine_create_video_renderer() demanded
  VIDEO_OUTPUT_FORMAT ("Output format was not specified."), create_topology() failed ("Failed to create simple video
  render node, hr 0x80004005"), nothing played, and UpdateVideoStream() was a stub. UXP's gray placeholder stayed.
  PS 2026 shows the same gray box on Neutron (same plugin, byte-identical mp4): old gap, not a 2027 regression.

Windows behavior:
  - IMFMediaEngineClassFactory::CreateInstance, Remarks: in rendering mode "the Media Engine renders both audio and
    video", to the window (MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_PLAYBACK_HWND) or DirectComposition visual the application provides;
    MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_FORMAT is Required in frame-server mode but Optional in rendering mode.
    https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/mfmediaengine/nf-mfmediaengine-imfmediaengineclassfactory-createinstance
  - IMFMediaEngineEx::UpdateVideoStream: pSrc = area of the frame shown (NULL = the entire frame), pDst = area of the
    window where the video is drawn, pBorderClr = border color; in rendering mode it repositions/repaints, all NULL
    repaints the most recent frame; in frame-server mode it has no effect.
    https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/mfmediaengine/nf-mfmediaengine-imfmediaengineex-updatevideostream

Fix (mfmediaengine only, no per-app logic):
  - Rendering mode with a valid PLAYBACK_HWND and no VIDEO_OUTPUT_FORMAT builds the existing frame sink with
    DXGI_FORMAT_B8G8R8X8_UNORM (system-memory RGB32 samples; the topology loader adds decoder + converter as for
    frame-server WIC transfers).
  - A presenter thread per rendering-mode engine shows each frame when the presentation clock reaches its time
    (video_frame_sink_get_pts, the same selection OnVideoStreamTick uses), and the current frame again on
    UpdateVideoStream. It draws with GDI (GetDC + StretchDIBits HALFTONE) into pDst (default: the client area), the
    source rect scaled with its aspect ratio kept, the rest of pDst filled with the border color when one was given.
  - UpdateVideoStream stores src/dst/border (src NULL = whole frame) and repaints; in frame-server mode returns S_OK
    (no effect) instead of E_NOTIMPL. Thread stopped on Shutdown and on final Release (5 s capped join).
  Logs: ERR "neutron-mfengine-hwnd: engine %p renders into hwnd %p." once per rendering-mode engine;
  "neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_MFENGINE_HWND = n" once per process.

Not covered / differs from Windows:
  - Windows presents through DXGI/DirectComposition; this draws with GDI into the window. The app's own WM_PAINT of
    that window can overwrite a frame until the next one (<= 1 frame period while playing; a paused frame comes back
    on the app's UpdateVideoStream). Under a layered (LWA_COLORKEY) parent -- UXP's tip popup uses key 0 -- pure-black
    video pixels would be keyed out by GDI; not seen with these clips (INFERRED risk, not measured).
  - MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_PLAYBACK_VISUAL (DirectComposition target) is still unimplemented (FIXME kept).
  - Rendering mode WITH a DXGI manager or an explicit VIDEO_OUTPUT_FORMAT takes the same GDI path (system-memory
    transfer); not exercised (UXP sets neither).
  - PS rich tool tooltips (also UXP <video>, e.g. crop-tool.mp4 with an AAC track) not reached in the lab (PS 2027
    toolbar hover opens the tool flyout instead); audio-track playback through this path not measured.

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-203pv = 203 + this mfmediaengine 64+32, prefix copies of the lab PS 2026+2027 prefix,
nested desk 175%, tip forced by deleting the PS Prefs.psp before each start; video area sampled in 3 captures ~1 s
apart: pixel std and frame-to-frame difference):
  - Base 203 (t2): gray 32,32,32, std 0, diff 0.
  - Kill switch NEUTRON_MFENGINE_HWND=0, same build: PS 2027 t6, t7, t10 + PS 2026 u2 -> 4/4 gray (std 0, diff 0).
  - Fix on: PS 2027 t4, t5, t8, t9 + PS 2026 u1, u3 -> 6/6 PLAYS (std 56-74, diff 39-82 between captures; the
    Generate Image clip visibly advancing, upright, filling the box). "Got it" dismisses; quits CLEAN; 0 page
    faults / Unhandled; no "did not stop".
  - Regression: Premiere 2026 (project si-pr-smoke2) on 203pv: opens, timeline plays (playhead 3:09 -> 7:09),
    quits CLEAN, 0 faults; it created no rendering-mode engine (no neutron-mfengine line). Static: among the
    installed Adobe binaries only UXP's dynamic-torqnative.dll references PLAYBACK_HWND in code; libcef/msedge
    (WebView2) and LrC's video_toolkit (frame-server help videos) do not contain the GUID at all.

Kill switch: NEUTRON_MFENGINE_HWND=0 (restores the old behavior: rendering mode fails topology creation).
